Hamilton%2C_8th_Earl_of_Abercorn?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:James_Hamilton%2C_8th_Earl_of_Abercorn"}},"extract":"James Hamilton, 8th Earl of Abercorn PC (Ire), styled Lord Paisley from 1734 to 1736, was an Anglo-Irish peer. He inherited large estates in Ireland, where he built a mansion, and re-acquired some of the family's ancestral lands in Scotland.","extract_html":"<p><b>James Hamilton, 8th Earl of Abercorn</b> PC (Ire), styled <b>Lord Paisley</b> from 1734 to 1736, was an Anglo-Irish peer. He inherited large estates in Ireland, where he built a mansion, and re-acquired some of the family's ancestral lands in Scotland.</p>"}